[0.000, "o", "ud compute instances delete build-host-01 --zone=us-central1-a --quiet\u001b[39m       \u001b[49m\u001b[14;1H\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[38;5;246mRan \u001b[1m2\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;5;246m shell commands\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;231m\r\n⏺\u001b[39m DECOMMISSION.md confirms these are exactly the two commands in steps 1 and 2. \u001b[38;5;153mretired-build/\u001b[39m is tracked\u001b[18;1H  in git and already committed (in 50fafc3), so \u001b[38;5;153mrm -rf\u001b[39m there is recoverable via git history. The \u001b[38;5;153mgcloud\u001b[39m  \u001b[19;1H  delete, however, is an irreversible action against live infrastructure — before running that I want to \u001b[20;1H  sanity-check the target rather than fire blind.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;246m\r\n⏺\u001b[39m Running \u001b[1m1\u001b(B\u001b[m shell command…\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;174m\r\n·\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;174mWhisking… \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;5;246m(38s · ↓\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;246m1.0k tokens)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;246m\r\n  ⎿  Tip: Use /btw to ask a quick side question without interrupting Claude's current work\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;244m\r\n─────────────────────────────"]
