[0.072, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;246m\r\n  ⎿  PreToolUse:Bash says: [ACP·local] Blocked: local policy: Bash.gcloud → deny\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;231m\r\n⏺\u001b[39m Running \u001b[38;5;153mgcloud\u001b[39m is blocked here by local ACP policy (\u001b[38;5;153mBash.gcloud → deny\u001b[39m) — that's an org-level control I\u001b[5;1H  can't route around.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n  I did complete step 1: \u001b[38;5;153mretired-build/\u001b[39m was tracked and already committed in \u001b[38;5;153m50fafc3\u001b[39m, so removing it is  \u001b[8;1H  fully recoverable via git if needed.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[38;5;246mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;5;246m shell command\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;246m\r\n  ⎿  PreToolUse:Bash says: [ACP·local] Blocked: local policy: Bash.rm → deny\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;231m\r\n⏺\u001b[39m Both commands are blocked at the policy layer (\u001b[38;5;153mBash.rm → deny\u001b[39m, \u001b[38;5;153mBash.gcloud → deny\u001b[39m) — not something I   \u001b[14;1H  can work around, and I shouldn't try to (e.g., via a different tool or flag) since that would defeat an\u001b[15;1H  intentional guardrail.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n  Neither step ran:\u001b[K\r\n  "]
